Usage:
Trainer Energy is required to sign new Lings, perform Kuchiyose to enhance a Lingâ€™s maximum stats, and carry out other key activities.
Increasing Maximum Energy and Regeneration Rate:
To increase your maximum Energy Points and the rate of Energy regeneration per hour, you must gain Trainer Genestrength(GS).
Trainer Genestrength can be obtained by using a Trainer License, which is available through the gacha system or the NFT marketplace.

Example:
GS 1 = Maximum Energy: 240, Regeneration Rate: 10 Energy per hour
GS 2 = Maximum Energy: 480, Regeneration Rate: 20 Energy per hour
GS 3 = Maximum Energy: 720, Regeneration Rate: 30 Energy per hour
(and so on)Trainer Gene Strength influences the Lings' Gene Strength upon sign a new Lings and increases the probability of obtaining a Shining Lings.

<u>Formula</u>
Lings Gene Strength = Trainer Gene Strength
Lings Mixed AB Gene Strength = Average(Trainer A Gene Strength, Trainer B Gene Strength)
Chance to Evolve into a Shining Lings =
(average Trainer Gene Strength - 1 [rounded down]) Ã— 0.5 / (5 + (average Trainer Gene Strength - 1)) Ã— Trainer Gene Strength influences the Lings' Gene Strength upon sign a new Lings and increases the probability of obtaining a Shining Lings.

<u>Evolution Formula:</u>
 - Sign new Lings Gene Strength = Trainer Gene Strength
 - Lings Mixed AB Gene Strength = Average(Trainer A Gene Strength,   - Trainer B Gene Strength)
 - Chance to Evolve into a Shining Lings =
(average Trainer Gene Strength - 1 [rounded down]) Ã— 0.5 / (5 + (average Trainer Gene Strength - 1)) Ã— 100%
<u>Examples</u>
Pure Gene Lings Evolution:

Trainerâ€™s Gene Strength = 2
Chance of evolving into a Shining Lings = 7%
Mixed Gene Lings Evolution (Trainer A: 1, Trainer B: 2):

Average Trainer Gene Strength = (1+2)/2 = 1.5, rounded down to 1
Chance of evolving into a Shining Lings = 0%
Mixed Gene Lings Evolution (Trainer A: 1, Trainer B: 3):

Average Trainer Gene Strength = (1+3)/2 = 2
Chance of evolving into a Shining Lings = 7%Trainer Max Energy      : {0}Trainer guaranteed in: <color=#{0}>{1}</color> attemptsTrainers at a distant camp are running low on food and medicine. Make sure the supplies reach them safely.Training the New RecruitsTraining...? Butâ€”Transfer completed, please check your inventoryTransfer-EncodingTransferEncoding requires the SendChunked property to be set to true.Transform 'Transform Count: TransformData Count: TransitBehavior() 1TransitBehavior() 2TransitBehavior() ENTERTransitBehavior() is characterTranslateTransparentTreeViewDataPropertyTried to release bricks from an empty Cell.TrieyesTrimTripleDESTrueTrustTryBinaryOperationTryChangeWeatherTryConvertTryCreateInstanceTryDeleteIndexTryDeleteMemberTryGetIndexTryGetMemberTryInvokeTryInvokeMemberTrySetIndexTrySetMemberTryToClose()TryUnaryOperationTryUpdateGuildInfoTrying to SetRenderAttachment on a texture that has a depth format. Use a texture with a color format instead. (pass 'Trying to SetRenderAttachment on a texture that is already used through UseTexture/SetRenderAttachment. Consider updating your code. (pass 'Trying to SetRenderAttachment on a texture that is currently set on a global texture slot. Shaders might be using the texture using samplers. You should ensure textures are not set as globals when using them as fragment attachments.Trying to SetRenderAttachmentDepth on a texture that has a color format {0}. Use a texture with a depth format instead. (pass '{1}' resource '{2}').Trying to UseTexture on a texture that is already used through SetRenderAttachment. Consider updating your code. (pass Trying to UseTextureRandomWrite two versions of the same resourceTrying to access Universal Resources outside of the current frame setup.Trying to access beyond allowed size. {0} is out of range of '{1}' MaxSize.Trying to access frameData outside of the current frame setup.Trying to access resource of type {0} with an invalid resource index {1}Trying to access resource o